    {
      "id": "p0077-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Early Japanese games could only support hiragana and/or katakana, but kanji became available as game hardware improved. Toby and 8-4 intentionally avoided heavy kanji usage in Undertale's dialogue to retain the game's intended \"retro\" vibe.",
        "raw": "Early Japanese games could only support hiragana and/or katakana,\nbut kanji became available as game hardware improved. Toby and 8-4\nintentionally avoided heavy kanji usage in Underta/e's dialogue to retain\nthe game's intended \"retro\" vibe.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12095813,
          0.27876429,
          0.67335088,
          0.34145
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11963418,
          0.27805,
          0.67467483,
          0.34252143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          11,
          12,
          13,
          14
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "早期日本游戏只能支持平假名或片假名，随着硬件进步，才逐渐用上汉字。Toby 与 8-4 有意避免在 Undertale 对白中大量使用汉字，以保留游戏原本想要的“复古”感。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
